A ``PERIOD`` value written with dates instead of date-times, such as ``RDATE;VALUE=PERIOD:19970101/19970102``, was accepted when a calendar was parsed and then raised an ``AttributeError`` when it was written out again, or a ``TypeError`` where only one half was a date. Such a value is now read as midnight, in the timezone of the other half where it has one. I used AI to assist me with this change. @lcampanella98
